<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">sharpen</ansi>

A whetstone puts an edge on a bladed weapon (slashing, cleaving, or
stabbing). A sharp blade does <ansi fg="yellow">+1 damage</ansi> on each strike that lands, for
its next 20 strikes. Then it's dull again. A warrior at the whetstone
makes the edge last longer (<ansi fg="command">help fieldsmith</ansi>).

A whetstone has 10 uses, and one use sharpens every blade one member has
equipped. Your whetstones sharpen your whole company, you first, then your
companions in order, until the uses run out. Blades that are still sharp
cost nothing. Whetstones are sold at the markets.

You can sharpen any time, except in the middle of a fight.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">sharpen</ansi>
  Sharpen your company's blades.

  <ansi fg="command">sharpen status</ansi>
  See whose blades are sharp, and how many whetstone uses you have.

  <ansi fg="command">sharpen auto on</ansi> / <ansi fg="command">sharpen auto off</ansi>
  Sharpen automatically at the end of each camp rest.

<ansi fg="command">camp sharpen</ansi> does the same at camp. <ansi fg="command">look</ansi> at a blade shows its edge.
